WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.980
<b>I want to be connected
A</b>

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.030
<i>Good morning!</i>

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.430
<i>Happy every day!</i>

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>Even happier with Lucky Selfies! 
Azuma Saradish!</i>

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.990
Any word from Kazuki?

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.090
Nothing since he messaged me last night 
saying he's staying at Enta-kun's.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.740
<i>Today's Lucky Selfie Item is...</i>

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:24.750
<b>Asakusa</b>

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.870
Come to think of it, they are kind of alike.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.190
Maybe that was why.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.500
<b>Lucky Selfie Fortunes</b>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.500
<b>Asakusa</b>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.500
<b><i>I take a bath twice a day, dish. Once right before I sleep and once after I wake up, dish.</i></b>

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:26.880
<b>Sachet</b>

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.500
Asakusa 
Sara
TV 

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.500
<i>Sachets?</i>

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.710
<i>Huh?</i>

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.510
<i>It's sachets again, dish.</i>

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.510
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.510
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.510
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.650
Kazu-chan!

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.180
He forgot this, dish.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.930
Thanks.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.150
Sure.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.630
<i>Another happy day.</i>

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.690
<i>Good Sarakku!</i>

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.690
Kazu-chan...

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.260
Kappas for life!

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.020
Cucumbers are so good!

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.200
They're so much better than when I'm human!

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.960
Yum, yum! Yum, yum, yum!

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.960
He's finally lost it.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.760
To the east, Kazuki-noumi...

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.520
To the west, Enta-yama...

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.770
What does sumo have to do with anything?

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.770
Ready...

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.580
Every... thing!

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.270
You're still in! You're still in! 
You're still in!

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.950
You're still in! You're still in! 
You're still in, kero.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.280
<i>My skin against Kazuki's...</i>

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.030
Show me what you've got.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.160
You're still in! You're still in!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.160
Kazuki...

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.410
I think I'm going to go crazy.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:08.040
We're the golden duo, aren't we?

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:08.730
You're still in! You're still in! 
You're still in!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.240
Oh, right, this again.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.870
Kazuki-noumi!

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.170
Enta...

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:16.730
Are you okay?

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:17.920
Are you hurt?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.670
Is this another fantasy?

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.050
Ow!

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.250
This is reality.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.010
Kappas for the win!

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.060
Kero!

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.070
<b>Where Did the Scent Pouches Go?</b>

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.030
<i>And now for the next story, dish.</i>

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.730
<i>The Asakusa Scent Pouch Incident 
continues from yesterday.</i>

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:39.630
<i>The Asakusa Police Department is 
investigating this as a possible act</i>

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.580
<i>of a large-scale robbery organization.</i>

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.320
<i>Sasheeeh!</i>

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.320
<b>Where Did the Scent Pouches Go?</b>

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.320
<i>Smells can be troublesome. I take a bath twice a day, dish.</i>

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:48.830
Hey, have the incidents ever been 
in the news two days in a row?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.830
<b>New Ningyoyaki Flavors!</b>

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.830
<i>Smells can be troublesome. I take a bath twice a day, dish.</i>

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.830
Come to think of it, they haven't.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.250
Wait, shoot!

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.450
I know!

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.340
If no one can see us in kappa form,

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.190
we could get into amusement parks for free.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.110
Found a ball!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.720
Where are we?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.230
This is where I always 
came to dress up as Sara.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.180
Kero!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.560
Cross-dressing as an idol, though...

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.380
Can you believe it? How stupid.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:13.740
Kero!

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.850
You worked pretty hard at it.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:17.660
And now, I kero!

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.990
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.860
All right, let's have fun!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.610
Kappas for the win!

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.360
Pole dance!

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.830
I can make a casual pass to Kazuki right now.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.870
Hey, Enta!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.750
Pass me the ball!

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.300
Are you sure?

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.750
You said it doesn't matter.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.000
It totally does.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.630
The golden duo is back together!

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.130
Kazuki...

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.510
Pass!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:51.520
Enta, a miracle shot for your heart!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
<b>Kyuri-ya</b>

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
<b>Hotel Kappa-en</b>

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:54.520
Kazuki!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:56.930
Nice!

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.280
Hey, Enta!

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.260
Aw, crap.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.530
All right.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.280
Pass!

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.280
Sorry, I gotta go to the bathroom.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.440
It's no use.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.630
He's only going to get worse.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.900
You don't need to tell me that.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.430
I know!

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.560
There's a good cucumber spot ahead.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.510
You like cucumbers, right?

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.560
What the hell is a cucumber spot?

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:39.190
Nyantaro! Come out!

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.360
He ran away.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.730
I thought so.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.740
Sorry I'm late, Nyantaro.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.250
Hey, Nyantaro...

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.000
Kazu-chan's coming home, right?

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.880
Please get my message.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.130
Huh?

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.140
I don't remember installing this app.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.420
Who's the bad little boy?

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.850
A policeman...

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.220
Are you here to arrest me?

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.280
What makes you think that?

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.660
Because I stole Kazu-chan's smile.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.770
Who's Kazu-chan?

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.660
My big brother.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.040
He hasn't been home since yesterday.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:37.480
Huh.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.930
We're in the same situation.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.790
My guy hasn't been back since yesterday.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.920
Are you a bad boy, too?

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.820
Of course not.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.390
<i>He's</i> the bad one.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:53.610
He's betraying me again, looking all cool.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:57.430
He's a doll whose emotions 
have fallen out of him.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:01.680
I want Kazu-chan to smile.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.940
Oh?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.700
Then why don't you show me 
whether what's inside you is

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:14.830
<b>Sleep</b>

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.830
desire or love?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.160
The future exists only for those 
who can connect their desires.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.710
Back down.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.970
Be honest with yourself already.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.980
Let me go.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.340
Haruka has nothing to do with me anymore.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.720
He's still—

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.240
Nyantaro?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.730
Haruka's gone.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.610
He's unconscious.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.870
Oh my God, that's creepy.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.200
What is wrong with you?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.030
Yes. Hello, kero?

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.690
Understood, kero.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:11.130
Yasaka Haruka has been 
taken by the Imperial Army, kero.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:12.770
Seriously?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.010
What's the Imperial Army?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:19.430
The enemy that destroyed the Kappa Kingdom.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.150
What's their goal?

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.520
Why are they taking people?

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.770
They kill them and turn 
them into kappa zombies.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.150
I won't let them!

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.030
I'm going to save Haruka.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.030
We were told not to act on our own.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.540
Asakusa Police Department  Kawauso Koban

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.540
Otter Police Box

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.540
<b>Traffic accident reports</b>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.540
<b>Deaths
Injuries</b>

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.540
Look who's talking.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.960
We'll open this door for you.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:51.440
<b>Extract</b>

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.300
Desire?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:55.310
Or love?

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.430
Desire extraction!

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.830
Otter Empire?!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:08.940
The otters and kappas have been 
at war for a long time, kero.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.280
Come with me, kero.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.220
Why did we have to get involved?

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:21.450
We were fighting over the desire 
energy of the Shirikodama, kero.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.120
Having taken all of the 
Kappa Kingdom's desire energy,

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.850
<b>Kappanokawa</b>

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.850
<b>Otternoyama</b>

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.850
<b>Otter Wins</b>

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.210
the Otter Empire next turned
 to the humans, kero.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:32.710
So you're a survivor of your doomed kingdom.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:39.470
I'm the only one that can
create Dishes of Hope, kero.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:43.730
If the empire were to find out, 
they would come for my life, kero.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.940
Where are we?

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:03.540
This is the Otter Empire's
 secret hideout, kero.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.390
Where's Haruka?

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:10.250
They put everything in boxes, kero.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.150
We have to open all of these boxes?

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.510
We don't have time for that!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.510
Hang on...

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.170
It's that one!

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:49.920
Stop!

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.260
The floor...

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.290
What now?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:59.460
Enta!

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:02.300
Go, Kazuki!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.800
Don't give up on Haruka!

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:03.800
Kero?!

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.200
Kuji!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.390
You still have time.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.200
So run!

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:41.940
Haruka!

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.090
I'm almost there!

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:50.230
Haruka!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.960
Haruka!

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.690
No...

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:04.740
It can't be.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.220
Do you want to save Yasaka Haruka, kero?

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.010
You can save him?

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:16.410
We can transplant your 
Shirikodama into him, kero.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:20.610
That way, Yasaka Haruka will 
be brought back to life, kero.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.630
Really?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.630
There's no other way, kero.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:25.850
Wait!

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.260
What happens to him if 
he loses his Shirikodama?

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:31.310
He's not going to die like 
the kappa zombies, is he?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.020
You can't do that!

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.860
Humans are connected through 
their Shirikodamas, kero.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.190
When they lose them, they become incapable 
of connecting with anyone else,

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.030
and they get kicked out of the 
circle that makes up the world.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.990
<b>Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt</b>

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:45.490
<b>Butt</b>

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.280
<b>No beginning</b>

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.280
<b>No connection</b>

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.280
<b>No end</b>

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.530
Outside of the circle...

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:55.290
Yasaka Kazuki will never have 
existed in this world, kero.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:13:01.550
Every memory, event and thing having to 
do with you will be completely undone, kero.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.230
What the hell?!

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:04.930
That's worse than dying!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.660
So all the kappa zombies we've defeated so far

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.430
have been erased from having ever existed?

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.430
Does that mean

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.650
Haruka's accident never 
will have happened, either?

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.190
It does, kero.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.970
I see.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.570
Right...

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.320
I want you to give Haruka my Shirikodama.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.160
All right, kero.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.120
Then jump into this pit, kero.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.080
Boop.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.330
We're going to cut the

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.590
connection between you and your 
Shirikodama for the transplant, kero.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.590
Got it.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.360
Kazuki! No!

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:47.970
Stay right there!

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.840
<i>I get it.</i>

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>I was always on the outside of the circle.</i>

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.730
<i>If I don't exist, everything will go well.</i>

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.730
<i>This is my last chance.</i>

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:03.730
<i>I can't connect, so it's the only 
way I can make things right.</i>

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:10.070
No, Kazuki!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.830
Do you really think this is 
going to make Haruka happy?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.260
It's fine.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:17.940
Haruka will forget everything and move on.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:18.990
So will you.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:21.170
You'll forget about me soon enough.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.110
How could I ever forget about you?

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:24.200
Stop!

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.010
Please, don't!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:25.670
Kazuki!

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:27.670
We won't catch up!

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.180
Kazuki!

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.190
Kazuki!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.450
Is he all right?

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.310
I think so.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.630
One, two...

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.810
Give me a break.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:55.830
Why?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.120
Why did you get in my way?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.870
I made this choice!

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:00.830
Leave me alone!

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:03.340
It's better if I don't exist!

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:09.340
Quit pissing me off with your miserable 
rambling and think of something else!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.590
He's right.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.350
I'm not letting you vanish!

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:17.980
Why?

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.340
I threw that out.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:21.540
Haruka left this to me.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.780
He never gave up on you!

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:26.370
He believes in you, and he's waiting.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.680
<i>Result: Love.</i>

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:28.800
Result

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.340
Love

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.990
<i>Box: Return.</i>

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:29.990
Box

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:29.990
Return

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:33.310
Oh?

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.990
He's still alive, kero.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.620
It's Haruka's box.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.130
Haruka!

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.890
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.890
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.890
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.390
<i>Dear Sara-chan.</i>

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.510
<i>This is my last message to you.</i>

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:09.400
<i>I had a lot of fun connecting
 with you every day.</i>

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:14.660
<i>Before we go, can I tell you my secret?</i>

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.470
<i>I've done something terrible.</i>

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:21.660
<i>I've hurt someone that my 
beloved big brother loves.</i>

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:24.080
That's not true, Haruka.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.170
That's not!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.910
<i>The reason I chased down Kazu-chan 
was because I was afraid.</i>

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.430
<i>I thought Kazu-chan might 
go somewhere far away.</i>

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.430
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.430
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.430
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:41.680
<i>That day, I picked up something 
Kazu-chan's real mother left behind.</i>

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.190
It smells the same as Kazu-chan.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:48.190
Hey, might you be Haruka-kun?

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:50.530
Don't take Kazu-chan!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.410
Go away!

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:52.940
Don't come back anymore!

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.450
<i>She smiled and said, 
"It's okay, don't worry."</i>

00:16:57.830 --> 00:16:59.790
<i>She looked just like Kazu-chan.</i>

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:05.830
<i>Kazu-chan stopped smiling after that,
and he threw out his miçanga.</i>

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:10.860
<i>I knew it was all my fault, 
but I wanted to be with Kazu-chan.</i>

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.270
<i>I wanted to see him smile.</i>

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:18.180
<i>I was so happy that he did what he did for me.</i>

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.750
<i>So I'm not going to give up.</i>

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.980
<i>Kazu-chan's coming home.</i>

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.730
<i>I have faith that he's going to smile again.</i>

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.240
Haruka!

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.300
Kazuki!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.070
It's no use!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.240
What do we do?

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.010
Shit, the only way we can go is back.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:50.250
It's a shredder.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:51.690
We don't have time.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.460
<b>Love</b>

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:55.260
Haruka's going to get minced.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.130
What do we do?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.510
Is there anything we can do?

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:00.930
Like what?!

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:07.910
I know this will be hard for you, 
but take this adorable body of mine and—

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.270
Catch, Jinnai!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.780
Pass it to Yasaka!

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.160
Make him stop the crane!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.340
But Kazuki...

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:22.410
Enta!

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:23.910
Pass it!

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:31.670
<i>He can be a bit stubborn, but Kazu-chan has 
a way of running straight for the goal.</i>

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.140
Kazuki! Catch it!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.300
Nice, Enta!

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:44.560
<i>He's a little hard to understand, but I 
know he's actually really kind and warm.</i>

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.560
Haruka!

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:50.560
I'm not going to give up on you anymore!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:15.310
<i>I'm not the only one who wants 
to see Kazu-chan's smile.</i>

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:19.450
<i>Kazu-chan, you're in the
middle of a big circle.</i>

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:27.720
W-We did it!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.520
It's gotten out again!

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.480
Sarazanmai!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.660
Desire assimilated.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.990
I'm a dead sachet.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.200
<b>Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Nioino    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt    Butt</b>

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:43.700
<b>Nioino</b>

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:44.490
<b>No beginning</b>

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:44.490
<b>No connection</b>

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:44.490
<b>No end</b>

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.490
<b>Students Crossing</b>

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.880
They stole our target away from us 
and even determined our whereabouts.

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.740
This error could jeopardize our mission, Reo.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.550
Chill out.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.540
It was love that the kid had.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.260
We have no use for such a thing.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.600
What is it, Reo?

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.500
I should thank that kid.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:09.470
I'm in luck.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.230
I've found you.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.230
It's our hope.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:16.350
This feels way more right.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:16.980
Agreed.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:21.020
And, uh, like... Sorry.

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:21.990
It's fine.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.990
Wouldn't you have preferred 
to stay a kappa, kero?

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.400
I feel weird.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:34.250
I'm the same as yesterday, 
yet it's like I'm a new being.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.000
But this is the real me.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.490
Thanks.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.020
I'm glad I have you guys.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:47.010
<b>I   W a n t   t o   C o n n e c t,</b>

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:47.010
<b>s o   I ' m   N o t   G i v i n g   U p</b>

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.080
<i>Stand by me</i>

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:52.080
<i>Please</i>

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:57.650
<i>I don't know if I can become stronger</i>

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:03.000
<i>The rain washes away my tears</i>

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:08.280
<i>I want to be embraced by your warmth</i>

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.710
<i>The flickering lightbulb that's been neglected</i>

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.710
<i>One morning, it had quietly died</i>

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.460
<i>It's almost like you and me</i>

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.210
<i>Like the fleeting moment when
we held our hands together</i>

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:27.840
<i>I sat with my arms around my knees</i>

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:31.430
<i>Thinking of the days long gone</i>

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:34.000
<i>Stand by me</i>

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:37.060
<i>Please</i>

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:42.290
<i>I don't know if I can become stronger</i>

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:47.900
<i>Even if you aren't here now</i>

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:53.570
<i>Please give me the courage to reach out</i>

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.450
<i>Stand by you</i>

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:59.580
<i>Please</i>

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:04.780
<i>I want to get rid of everything</i>

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:09.930
<i>The rain washes away my tears</i>

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:17.060
<i>I just want to be embraced by your warmth</i>

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.060
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.060
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.060
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:22.820
We've found you!

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:27.450
My desire is shattering!

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:30.950
D-D-Darkness!

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:31.910
Reo! Look out!

00:22:38.510 --> 00:22:39.810
Why...

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.830
Why would you protect me?

00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:44.760
Don't let go of your desires.

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:50.090
The future exists only for those 
who can connect their desires.

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:52.190
Mabu!

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.250
<b>This is a work of fiction.
